abacus	From Latin abacus, from Ancient Greek άβαξ (abax, "counting board"). Doublet of abaque.
bear	The animal: from Old English bera, of Germanic origin.	To carry: from Old English beran.
dog	From Middle English dogge, from Old English docga, of uncertain origin.
ice_cream	From ice + cream, attested from the 18th century.
